{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Split from silvern-dewy-damselfly (f4cf-60b2-41c0-4843) during its plan review.\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter a close whose completion-signature append failed, a later reader cannot reliably tell\nthat ticket apart from one closed with the gate off. Damselfly makes the loss machine-readable\nin the RETURNED PAYLOAD of the call that suffered it, but that payload is ephemeral — it is\nnever persisted (`_lib_writes.py:424`, `_commands/transition.py:591`,\n`schemas/transition_result.schema.json`). An agent that was not the caller, or the same agent\nin a later session, has no durable discriminator.\n\n## Premise verified in code — PARTIALLY true, narrower than first written\n\nThe original draft of this ticket claimed all three states are indistinguishable. That\noverstates it; verification found one existing discriminator:\n\n**The `COMPLETION_VERDICT` PASS sidecar** (`llm/completion_sidecar.py:202`\n`latest_pass_record`, tag `completion_verifier_pass_v1`) is emitted on EVERY completion PASS at\n`_commands/close_precheck.py:577-580`, before signing and before the close commits. So:\n\n| state | `attestations[\"completion-verifier\"]` | PASS sidecar |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) closed, attestation valid | present | present |\n| (b) closed, signature failed to persist | absent | **present** |\n| (c) closed, gate OFF | absent | absent |\n\n(b) is therefore already distinguishable via `audit/read.py:113-123,203-210`. Three caveats\nkeep it from being a real answer: the sidecar is **reducer-ignored**\n(`completion_sidecar.py:10-16` — not in `KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES`, so it never reaches compiled state\nand `rebar show` cannot see it, only the audit surface); its emit is **best-effort**, dropped\nwith only a stderr warning (`close_precheck.py:349-355`); and `prune()` deletes it after\n`RETAIN_PER_TICKET = 10` (`completion_sidecar.py:44,123`).\n\n**(c) has no discriminator at all, and that is the sharper bug.** The gate's on/off state at\nclose time is nowhere in the store — it is read from config and discarded\n(`_commands/close_precheck.py:410-416`; key `verify.require_completion_verification_for_close`\nat `_config_schema.py:159`, default False). So \"closed with no attestation\" collapses these\ninto ONE indistinguishable state:\n\n* gate genuinely off (`close_precheck.py:416`)\n* `--force` close (`close_precheck.py:417`)\n* config unreadable → `gate_enabled` **fails OPEN** (`_commands/gates.py:79-87`)\n* `source == \"local\"` unattested close (`close_precheck.py:585-586`)\n* `certifiable is False` withholding (`close_precheck.py:589-600`)\n* a dropped PASS sidecar\n\nWorse, `txn.transition_core` **accepts `force_close_reason` and never uses it** — the parameter\nat `_commands/txn.py:198` occurs exactly once in the file and is silently discarded, though\n`transition_close.py:474` passes it. A force close leaves no durable reason on the STATUS\nevent. (Tracked separately; see the linked bug.)\n\nThe close STATUS event records only `status`, `current_status`, `parent_status_uuid`, and\npresent-only `close_class` (`txn.py:277-296`; documented `docs/event-schema.md:47`).\n\n## Direction\n\nRecord the EXPECTATION and its outcome on the close STATUS event — the same locked write that\nalready commits the close (`txn.transition_core`), so NO additional lock acquisition is needed.\nThis is the point: an audit comment or a second event would append through the same\n`event_append` -> `write_lock` path whose 60s timeout causes the very failure being recorded,\nand would be missing exactly when it matters.\n\nA reader then compares \"a completion signature was expected\" against \"a valid completion\nattestation exists\", and gate-off reads as not-expected rather than as an indistinguishable\nabsence. This is an event-schema addition: field on the STATUS event, reducer handling, and\n`docs/event-schema.md`, versioned so an older reader that does not know the field degrades\nsafely (the preserved-and-ignored precedent the sidecar already follows).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A close that expected a completion signature records that expectation durably in the\n      SAME locked write as the STATUS event, with no additional lock acquisition — verified by\n      a test asserting no extra write-lock is taken\n- [ ] A later reader, holding no lock and reading only reduced state, distinguishes\n      closed-and-signed from closed-with-signature-lost from closed-with-gate-off — verified\n      by a test closing one ticket each way\n- [ ] The `--force`, local-source, and certifiable-false closes are not reported as gate-off —\n      verified by a test\n- [ ] The added field is documented in `docs/event-schema.md` and an older reader that does\n      not know it degrades safely — verified by a test"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786562677242325001,"uuid":"d1cd35df-f577-42d3-bfea-978c09a076b7"}